# Line endings are decided here, not by whoever cloned the repo.
#
# Without this file, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF in the working tree while
# the blobs stay LF. Prettier's endOfLine:"auto" then infers per file from what it finds, and any
# file that ends up MIXED - a CRLF checkout patched by a tool that writes LF - fails
# `npm run format:check` locally while CI, which checks out LF-only, prints a pass. A red gate that
# only one machine can see is the kind that gets dismissed as noise.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` makes every text file LF in the working tree too, on every platform, so what
# the formatter checks is what the repository holds. Scoped to frontend/ because this directory is
# also published as the ROOT of a separate repository, where a root .gitattributes would not travel.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never normalized, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
